    Keep evidence-less closures visible and the case collector crash-free
    
    Addendum/evidence files are stored beside case objects and one live addendum is
    a top-level JSON list. read() therefore returned a list, and reconcile() died
    on .get(), leaving index.json stale. Guard non-dict records without treating
    them as cases, and filter the index inputs to real case objects.
    
    Also surface historical verified_closed cases that carry no case-bound closure
    artifact under unresolved_without_closure_evidence. This does not reopen or
    rewrite any case object and does not change open-case dispatch; it keeps the
    obligation discoverable until an authorized reconciliation supplies evidence,
    as Act 23 §5.1/§7 require. On a copy of the live store this lists nine
    historical evidence-less closures and exits 0.
    
    Extend the institutional smoke test with a non-case addendum record and a
    historical closure, asserting the addendum is preserved byte-for-byte, the
    collector exits 0, and the closure remains listed as unresolved.

